          <!--
            No CenterOn and no ZoomToLevel here on purpose, and that is worth a sentence.

            Those two are operations: they run every frame, so a patch holding them pins the view on
            every frame and the map cannot be dragged - which is exactly what HowTo Show a map is
            for, where driving the view from IOBoxes is the lesson.

            This patch is about a shape sitting on the map, and you cannot see that unless you can
            move the map. So the starting view comes from the Map node's Initial pins instead: they
            are applied once, through Home, and then leave the viewport alone.
          -->
          <Pad Id="JXt620dcIwTNKf5ghwhaGp" Comment="Diagnostics" Bounds="236,873,35,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="True">
